I have been playing the Mac version of 2.3 and I seem to have discovered
something which my friend claims has never been mentioned on this
newsgroup.  

When you are polymorphed into a human and are asked what your new name
is, it seems that your choice can have quite interesting effects.  The
first time it happened, I tried Roland, and got 18/** strength.  This
has not proved to be consistent, but certain other names have gotten me
strengths on the same order.  I tried Caesar, Alexander, Gilgamesh,
Goliath, Gandalf, and Superman, among others.  Most of these gave me
18/** strength, except for Gandalf.  Superman seems to work more
consistently than the others.  My friend said that Gandalf gave him 
and 18 intelligence and lots of other good stats in 3.0, but I haven't
tried it yet.

Also, certain names seem to be effective when you are turned into a new
woman.  I got 18/** for Wonder Woman, Bodaecia, and 18/98 for Cleopatra.
I next tried Elizabeth, as in the English Queen, and got an 18/98. 
However, when I looked at my status line a little later, I noticed that
I was 12th level.  I believe this had something to do with the name
choice, as I was only on the 6th level and hadn't obtained any gain
level potions that I can remember.  I think it may have doubled my
level, but I haven't been able to test this yet.  The next time I tried
Elizabeth I was second level and it reduced me to first, so if this 
is indeed a feature of the game, it probably works only once per user.

Also, could someone tell me what the significance is of the name you 
give your dog?


